#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100959 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100801 :question/id #uuid "1228900d-87d4-5ff0-8e01-ff9417e82220" :question/math-academy-id "e-9978" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y = e^x + 1$\n\n- $y = -e^x$\n\n- $y = 2e^x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y = e^x + 1,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ {e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}{e}^{x}+1 \\\\ 0 & \\ne 1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y = e^x+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y = -e^x,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = -e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ -{e}^{x} & =-{e}^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y = -e^x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y = 2e^x,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 2{e}^{x} & =2{e}^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y = 2e^x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10dd2375-3309-5242-9f4a-93a4d27c3816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437992} {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f260d360-832c-5eaf-a407-8777898370d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} {:answer/id #uuid "44b02a34-b812-5969-824c-b1a36338dbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8de5f6f-2c45-581c-b864-deb370031b0b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} {:answer/id #uuid "977a699e-8cdd-54d7-b2cb-49b49d93ef59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} :answer-field/id #uuid "f011be38-b8ff-5f20-b55b-d93017ba44c0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e22d897d-f7ce-5b4f-b6d4-aa4c45c66b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141096" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$\n- **II.** $y=-2{e}^{x}$\n- **III.** $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{-2x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{-2x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{x}) \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 6{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{e}^{-x}+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(2{e}^{-x}+1) \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-4{e}^{-x}-2 \\\\ 2{e}^{-x} & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "babc8bec-aec4-50b2-983c-a5c5e19babf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438580} {:answer/id #uuid "0e681d75-6b90-5dfe-a3b1-fa927459e41a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e681d75-6b90-5dfe-a3b1-fa927459e41a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438581} :answer-field/id #uuid "008e9eb2-6761-57ab-9978-fe105459b52b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276e25b7-9187-5abb-9fa1-e532f9e988be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438582} {:answer/id #uuid "d44e3b64-6a02-5556-acfb-ebac7d16150e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276e25b7-9187-5abb-9fa1-e532f9e988be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438582} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b80ace-4085-5ca5-b15f-49cdc840fdc8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9303d64-f302-585f-918a-f75cda94e15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438584} {:answer/id #uuid "1db5d556-052a-51c4-994e-edad39635f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9303d64-f302-585f-918a-f75cda94e15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438584} :answer-field/id #uuid "997a3d7e-abcd-5f9a-bdb1-6ad87c83170f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a773fc2b-812d-5f5c-8cbb-9b1672c48928" :question/math-academy-id "q-79335" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y}{x}-2,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=2x$\n- **II.** $y={x}^{2}$\n- **III.** $y={x}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot 2x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}4-2 \\\\ 2 & =2.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{2},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}2x-2 \\\\ 0 & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y={x}^{2}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{3},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}2{x}^{2}-2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ne -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{3}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6c667e6-310e-5bb3-abf7-6315816cc3b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437974} {:answer/id #uuid "db3fe3a6-70e3-5cce-8c97-d3259c62d677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db3fe3a6-70e3-5cce-8c97-d3259c62d677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437975} :answer-field/id #uuid "63194eb9-d476-519a-91f1-8caa84c9e521" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae3abeb4-8839-5211-a768-11057573634d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437976} {:answer/id #uuid "f012982e-627f-59eb-84ad-762b4568f3ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3abeb4-8839-5211-a768-11057573634d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437976} :answer-field/id #uuid "566d8174-6351-5c75-b0e9-eb5a68f640f6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30de8136-a64d-55ca-874e-99d7fd9ffc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437978} {:answer/id #uuid "c1bc8de1-5d6d-553a-9b99-6f5e3f57a058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1bc8de1-5d6d-553a-9b99-6f5e3f57a058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437979} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e846ba-51fc-5861-b0ff-f945cc525241" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e106766c-2780-56ea-8754-563b11d222dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-141091" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- **II.** $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$\n- **III.** $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1)\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ 0 & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡2x \\\\ -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbde5cd7-4a4c-5937-a799-7b21b57c33b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437980} {:answer/id #uuid "db8c300c-0173-5e9e-b3c1-643f3e71fb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db8c300c-0173-5e9e-b3c1-643f3e71fb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437981} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed6b1190-4430-5c26-820c-6d5d6fae3d79" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaaedefb-b6d0-54a6-a654-e0dd3e7a6751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437982} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3e78e1-78cd-5462-9d85-a307e70a00d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b3e78e1-78cd-5462-9d85-a307e70a00d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437983} :answer-field/id #uuid "b282c918-c5d5-512d-9072-bda4c5f527ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "799580fd-342b-5be6-99a0-dd688980c5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437984} {:answer/id #uuid "3e846cbd-10b7-538f-889d-dfae8cd2b98f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e846cbd-10b7-538f-889d-dfae8cd2b98f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437985} :answer-field/id #uuid "178b5312-5ff7-5d13-a367-0d4394cd147d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6e3bd06-ef25-5819-bfee-624e8862d278" :question/math-academy-id "q-141092" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **II.** $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c3ad39e-a247-5a6c-ba6f-410a6f727d7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437986} {:answer/id #uuid "8375a5f9-1e5b-5e68-a1a2-d4bb22077aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c3ad39e-a247-5a6c-ba6f-410a6f727d7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437986} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d0a85f4-6b7a-5206-8912-5ef75d07d5c7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "810eaa21-f1bd-5e35-9c60-fc5b515f7263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437988} {:answer/id #uuid "15681334-eb31-5858-ab81-367c516d43bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15681334-eb31-5858-ab81-367c516d43bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437989} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e12c95-c280-5407-b364-8a9b3e68d6ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e897d7-5a49-5a79-afb7-d23418de5981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437990} {:answer/id #uuid "ea53d260-6324-5283-bfa1-49a75c62e26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13e897d7-5a49-5a79-afb7-d23418de5981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437990} :answer-field/id #uuid "009959a9-26dc-55b5-b0de-6355e0fb41ca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c4f3444-d6eb-515b-bbe6-1939e7e4a2dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-141093" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}}.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **II.** $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **III.** $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{x}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 1 & =2\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true.* Therefore, the function $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{-1/2})}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{x}^{-1/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & =2\\sqrt{x} \\\\ -1 & =2x\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae46f16b-4a3a-5162-a76c-6350bbe8cf5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437998} {:answer/id #uuid "58700634-f044-5904-a864-1876384d88f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae46f16b-4a3a-5162-a76c-6350bbe8cf5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437998} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b224f9d-3166-5fdb-baba-fa61f05f4f1b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce64757c-e188-5d41-b4db-34bc0bbbcf38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438000} {:answer/id #uuid "cf78f6f1-2657-554f-8a9c-1247c354a4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce64757c-e188-5d41-b4db-34bc0bbbcf38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438000} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d71f85-f59a-5cf7-b850-1dadf02668b3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be0e6097-b578-52d5-9150-71d77d18a246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438002} {:answer/id #uuid "e02a6066-d8bf-5b4d-9ef9-11f939e2bf38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be0e6097-b578-52d5-9150-71d77d18a246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438002} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fa08ec6-f0a6-5680-8d5b-d98b9ec07792" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fbaad5c7-c732-5938-9213-ace2aa1f23df" :question/math-academy-id "q-141098" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=4x$\n- **II.** $y=2{x}^{2}$\n- **III.** $y={x}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=4x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ 4 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4(4x)}{x} \\\\ 4 & \\ne 16.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y=4x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{x}^{2},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ 4x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4(2{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ 4x & \\overset{?}{=}8x \\\\ -4x & \\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{x}^{2}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{3},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\ne 4{x}^{2} \\\\ 0 & \\ne {x}^{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{3}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "282c0558-4ce8-5a0b-9ecb-c71054b4d633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438004} {:answer/id #uuid "e16713e8-3c99-5127-b858-09f6a836bf7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282c0558-4ce8-5a0b-9ecb-c71054b4d633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438004} :answer-field/id #uuid "66cce0c8-4d30-5e9d-9a30-1ffdbfa68830" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ecffcc8-53d2-55a3-902f-3663dafe2076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438006} {:answer/id #uuid "3ecb31ee-bc9e-50df-bac9-69db3dc932bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ecb31ee-bc9e-50df-bac9-69db3dc932bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438007} :answer-field/id #uuid "272b3862-8779-5572-983f-8c22da89800f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0b1a108-8e14-51d7-8324-6b5a5d23d1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438008} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2c0aaa-91fa-53d3-af26-2a7cada1ff1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c2c0aaa-91fa-53d3-af26-2a7cada1ff1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438009} :answer-field/id #uuid "92920a70-1e81-5dc7-b31f-286893c6762f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b4e4e14-2aab-5c49-ba69-c1255e3d6145" :question/math-academy-id "q-141099" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$\n- **II.** $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$\n- **III.** $y=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\frac{1}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{2(-\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ 0 & \\ne \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{2(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true.* Therefore, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{2(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true.* Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e628123d-1857-59cf-99c8-dbfd81aafe1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438010} {:answer/id #uuid "344cc356-0f50-5320-b862-9a02d76becb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "344cc356-0f50-5320-b862-9a02d76becb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438011} :answer-field/id #uuid "1564794d-6e53-5ee1-997b-519c929759c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc4e1b4b-a13b-5770-acd6-294469c6028f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438012} {:answer/id #uuid "77177cda-2e58-507e-9d06-ce458fb9caf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc4e1b4b-a13b-5770-acd6-294469c6028f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438012} :answer-field/id #uuid "23bab858-62bf-5d21-a329-04f6739fb0c9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa0067b5-7621-5c0c-8653-7f4fab1a1f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438014} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7a4f50-4994-5270-b630-a3af98b9e734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa0067b5-7621-5c0c-8653-7f4fab1a1f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438014} :answer-field/id #uuid "92607fb9-865c-5419-afe4-0e52eddfcb38" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1646b369-92a0-554a-b444-f79313d419b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141101" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y={x}^{5}$\n- **II.** $y={x}^{10}$\n- **III.** $y=5{x}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{5},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{4}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 5{x}^{4} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5({x}^{5})}{x} \\\\ 5{x}^{4} & =5{x}^{4}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={x}^{5}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{10},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=10{x}^{9}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5({x}^{10})}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}5{x}^{9} \\\\ 5{x}^{9} & \\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{10}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=5{x}^{4},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{3}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5(5{x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}25{x}^{3} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 5{x}^{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=5{x}^{4}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdfdbbc9-8f7d-5b92-8c7a-21414891f782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438016} {:answer/id #uuid "f743e73c-1c1c-57a4-b868-2061d59c13d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdfdbbc9-8f7d-5b92-8c7a-21414891f782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438016} :answer-field/id #uuid "24dc77ad-6b0f-53af-88f4-af540b972387" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eed5f60f-41ca-59be-9206-62cf3368db12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438018} {:answer/id #uuid "211fe2a1-b60d-589d-aa08-14fd0a1d5134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eed5f60f-41ca-59be-9206-62cf3368db12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438018} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff89b593-0f13-5e74-b5fd-46b080b4539e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08076568-a59d-5e86-b097-716389e2ca49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438020} {:answer/id #uuid "38a8f5c4-ee71-5b43-b766-82516de6631a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08076568-a59d-5e86-b097-716389e2ca49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438020} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc38cc1b-44bf-5b80-afd0-c4f4a940e99f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8ec718b-9c17-5ad2-8af8-895d469a7090" :question/math-academy-id "q-141103" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{3y}}.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **II.** $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **III.** $y=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{3y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{3y}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{3(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{-3})}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{x}^{-3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & ={x}^{3} \\\\ -1 & ={x}^{4}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{3y}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{3(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{-6})}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{x}^{-6}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{x} & ={x}^{6} \\\\ -2 & ={x}^{7}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "905e51f9-40b0-5499-8af5-872dc35779be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438568} {:answer/id #uuid "70569d18-b405-5c62-a953-d3cd6b0b4af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "905e51f9-40b0-5499-8af5-872dc35779be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438568} :answer-field/id #uuid "e56acec3-06c5-5f56-bd10-ea20f7c101e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27cb07db-d269-5128-aef0-058e9346c8d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438570} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b0d574-6237-55e7-8ae6-4df3f29efc4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8b0d574-6237-55e7-8ae6-4df3f29efc4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438571} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b78d205-6f1a-546b-a4c3-a766d737c1e0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab214efc-6a3b-5507-98c5-f553f6d6c683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438572} {:answer/id #uuid "12509a84-7b4f-519d-a728-f34ffb63a683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab214efc-6a3b-5507-98c5-f553f6d6c683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438572} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6078f73-1ba1-5ea4-b78b-ee1956184333" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33546fc8-b13b-5d05-a639-8809e08f2462" :question/math-academy-id "q-79330" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y={e}^{-4x}$\n- **II.** $y={e}^{4x}$\n- **III.** $y=4{e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{-4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ -4{e}^{-4x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{-4x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 8{e}^{-4x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{4x} & =4{e}^{4x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={e}^{4x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=4{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4(4{e}^{x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}16{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 12{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=4{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19979361-a8df-557d-82d0-af8fd1cd5d48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438574} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c92711-50d6-5a72-8bfe-847ca17732fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c92711-50d6-5a72-8bfe-847ca17732fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef534af-2098-561e-b179-3f55b5991272" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c1b3ff-9199-58c6-8074-ef77f3973076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438576} {:answer/id #uuid "81f1c637-5060-5374-898f-afcdf1cec8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81f1c637-5060-5374-898f-afcdf1cec8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438577} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7782cf-bc1c-5aca-a517-f8894341953d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7481b3-4b8f-5e17-a81a-78de2657429f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438578} {:answer/id #uuid "b09ebf27-8594-5384-8496-cf3a363bb462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b09ebf27-8594-5384-8496-cf3a363bb462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438579} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b6785e8-bf84-599d-a8f6-c5925f0b9071" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2809b1ba-af02-5b95-b4d7-d9885f873cd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-79333" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=\\frac{7}{x}$\n- **II.** $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$\n- **III.** $y=\\frac{2}{x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{7}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{7}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\frac{1}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=\\frac{2}{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\frac{2}{x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to First-Order Differential Equations"}]}
